From 5be88d557ffe9c07ad8cabaadf54062837f40efe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:12:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/47] Nikon Z 6III (EXPEED 7) RTOS research machine

Add one new TCG-only machine, `nikon-z63`, which boots the factory RTOS
image ("eg") of a Nikon Z 6III, on top of QEMU 10.2.4:

  hw/arm/nikon-z63.c                           new, ~3100 lines
  run-z63.sh                                   new, launcher script
  hw/arm/Kconfig                               config NIKON_Z63
  hw/arm/meson.build                           build the new file
  configs/devices/aarch64-softmmu/default.mak  enable it in aarch64-softmmu

The machine models the DRAM map, a GICv3 distributor plus four redistributor
frames, the nkj UART console, the boot mailbox and CPU release register, and
the main DMA banks. Everything outside an explicitly modeled region is left
unmodeled on purpose: an access there is logged with its PC and stops the VM
instead of returning an invented device response, which is the intended
modelling workflow. The image starts at EL3 and drops to EL1 by itself.

The RTOS image is not included; point $EG at your own copy before running
run-z63.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <redacted-063e40a441cf@private.invalid>
